# Sample Webapp

This is the sample web app repository created by [LoKO](https://getloko.dev) to validate your GitOps flow.

It is a minimal static web page served by BusyBox `httpd`, wired end-to-end with:

- A container registry at `{{ container_registry_url }}`
- A GitOps repository managed by {{ provider }}
- Forgejo Actions CI running on `loko-runner`

Once you are comfortable with the setup, replace this app with your own and keep the same GitOps structure.

## Repository Structure

```
src/                    # Static web app source
Dockerfile              # Builds the BusyBox `httpd` image
.forgejo/workflows/
├── build.yaml                  # Build and push image on push to main
├── pr.yaml                     # Build and push PR preview image
└── promote.yaml                # Promote image tag from dev to prod
```

## CI Workflows

### Build (`build.yaml`)

Triggers on push to `main` when `src/**` or `Dockerfile` changes.

1. Builds the Docker image and tags it `main-<sha>`.
2. Pushes the image to `{{ container_registry_url }}/{{ app_repo }}`.
3. Clones the GitOps repo and updates the `newTag` in `apps/sample-webapp/overlays/dev/kustomization.yaml`.
4. Commits and pushes — {{ provider }} picks up the change and deploys to dev.

The app is available at: `https://webapp-dev.{{ apps_domain }}`

### PR Build (`pr.yaml`)

Triggers on pull requests to `main`.

Builds a PR image tagged `pr-{N}-<sha>` to validate PR changes. The image is pushed only
when a preview has been requested, and rebuild/push is skipped when that exact tag already
exists in the registry.
{% if provider == "fluxcd" %}
**Flux — label-driven trigger:**
Flux preview builds use two labels:

- `preview`: preview requested, push allowed after a successful build
- `preview-built`: preview image for the current PR SHA is ready to deploy

The workflow builds on matching PR code changes only when the current `pr-{N}-<sha>` image
does not already exist. When `preview` is present and the build succeeds, it pushes the
image, sets `preview-built`, and the
`ResourceSetInputProvider` in the GitOps repo selects that PR for preview deployment.

To trigger a preview:
1. Open a PR.
2. CI builds the image on matching PR code changes if that exact PR image tag is not already in the registry.
3. Add the `preview` label when you want to deploy a preview.
4. If the PR is already open, comment `/preview` to trigger the preview build immediately.
5. CI sets `preview-built` after a successful push.
6. Flux creates a namespace and deploys the preview.
7. Preview is available at `https://webapp-pr-{N}.{{ preview_domain }}`.
8. Remove `preview-built`, or close/merge the PR, to tear down the preview.

{% else %}
**ArgoCD — title-based trigger:**
The workflow builds on matching PR code changes only when the current `pr-{N}-<sha>` image
does not already exist. It only pushes the image and marks the PR deployable when `preview`
is present. The `ApplicationSet` gitea generator polls
Forgejo every 5 minutes and creates a preview environment for PRs whose title ends with
`[preview-built]`.

To trigger a preview:
1. Open a PR.
2. CI builds the image on matching PR code changes if that exact PR image tag is not already in the registry.
3. Add the `preview` label when you want to deploy a preview.
4. If the PR is already open, comment `/preview` to trigger the preview build immediately.
5. After a successful push, CI appends ` [preview-built]` to the PR title.
6. ArgoCD creates an Application named `webapp-pr-{N}` within ~5 minutes.
7. Preview is available at `https://webapp-pr-{N}.{{ preview_domain }}`.
8. Close or merge the PR to prune the preview Application.
{% endif %}

### Promote (`promote.yaml`)

Triggers manually via `workflow_dispatch`.

Promotes an image tag from dev to prod by updating `apps/sample-webapp/overlays/prod/kustomization.yaml` in the GitOps repo. If no tag is provided, the current dev tag is used.

## GitOps Repo

The Kubernetes manifests and overlays for this app live in the GitOps repository:

```
apps/sample-webapp/
├── base/               # Deployment, Service, Ingress
└── overlays/
    ├── dev/            # Dev overlay (updated automatically by CI)
    ├── prod/           # Prod overlay (updated via promote workflow)
    └── preview/        # PR preview overlay
```

The GitOps repo is at: `{{ forgejo_base_url }}/{{ forgejo_org }}/gitops`
